anching network of blood vessels, lymphatic vessels, or nerves. The nerves are typically axons outside the central nervous system."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plexus"},{"title":"Chakra","blocks":[{"text":"A chakra is a meditation-aid in the form of a psychic or psychospiritual energy-center in the subtle body, as visualized in a variety of Hindu and Buddhist tantric yoga and meditation practices."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chakra"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Gray848.png/500px-Gray848.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Gray848.png/500px-Gray848.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray848.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Celiac_plexus_coronal.png/500px-Celiac_plexus_coronal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Celiac_plexus_coronal.png/500px-Celiac_plexus_coronal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Approximate location of the celiac plexus on the coronal plane","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeliac_plexus_coronal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Gray849.png/500px-Gray849.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Gray849.png/500px-Gray849.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lower half of right sympathetic cord","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray849.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Yajna1.jpg/500px-Yajna1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser